      "key": "SFCC-7",
      "summary": "Search & Recommendations",
      "description": "Epic Summary\n\n\nThis epic delivers Zimmermann's end-to-end search and product discovery experience on SFCC, powered by Salesforce Einstein natively within the platform. It covers keyword search with predictive autocomplete, faceted filtering and sort on search results pages, zero-results handling, and AI-driven product recommendations across the PDP, cart, mini-bag, and account surfaces. The outcome is a seamless, discoverable product experience across all 8 regional storefronts that drives engagement and conversion.\nBusiness Value / Objective\n\n\nZimmermann currently relies on Searchspring/Athos Commerce for search and merchandising across all storefronts. Moving to Salesforce Einstein consolidates search natively within SFCC, eliminating a third-party dependency and giving the Site Merchandiser team direct control over search configuration, synonym rules, sorting, and AI-driven recommendations through Business Manager — without relying on a separate platform. This supports Zimmermann's strategic goals of improving conversion rate, reducing operational complexity, and enabling AI-driven personalisation.\nScope\nIn Scope\nSalesforce Einstein configuration for search indexing, autocomplete, recommendations, and AI-driven product ordering — replacing Searchspring/Athos Commerce across all 8 storefronts\nKeyword search across all product attributes (name, description, colour, size, material), real-time ranked results\nAutocomplete: two-panel layout (keyword suggestions + product grid), Popular Searches, category shortcut links, \"View All\" link, local currency pricing in results\nFocused/empty search state: Popular Searches, category navigation shortcuts, product grid\nSearch results page: product grid, result count display, breadcrumb, filter panel (reusing SFCC-108 Filters & Facets UI Component built in SFCC-6) and sort control (reusing SFCC-189 Sort Options UI Component built in SFCC-6)\nZero-results page: search term display, zero count, curated fallback product module, alternative search term suggestion, navigational shortcuts, inline search input\nMerchandiser controls: search redirects, synonym/dictionary rules, search ranking rules, Popular Search curation in Business Manager\nRecommendations: \"You May Also Like\" (YMAL) carousel on PDP, cart, mini-bag, and My Account; \"Complete the Look\" cross-sell on PDP, cart, mini-bag; \"Recently Viewed\" on PDP, PLP and cart; add-to-bag/wishlist directly from recommendation carousels\nEinstein AI-driven merchandising for automated product ordering on sub-category pages\nRules-based fallback configuration at launch, to activate until sufficient Einstein behavioural data accumulates\nRecommendation configuration: mix of AI-driven and rules-gated logic, configurable by season and category in Business Manager\nOut of Scope\nPLP build, product tile components, hero image, editorial slots, model/item toggle, category subcategory links, and PLP-specific filter panel — all covered in SFCC-6 Product Listing Page (PLP)\nProduct feed exports to Feedonomics and Lengow (scheduled BM jobs) — covered in SFCC-4 Product Catalogue\nPDP page build — covered in SFCC-5 Product Detail Page (PDP)\nSearchspring/Athos Commerce decommission (Zimmermann responsibility)\nEinstein configuration tuning and ongoing optimisation post-launch (Zimmermann)\nGTM/analytics tagging on search events — covered in SFCC-22 SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing\nDependencies\nSFCC-4 Product Catalogue — product attribute schema and catalogue data must be live in SFCC before search indexing and facet configuration can begin\nSFCC-6 Product Listing Page (PLP) — filter/facet UI components built in the PLP epic are reused on the search results page; sequencing must be aligned\nSFCC-18 Pricing — target-currency prices must be included in the SFCC search index for price-based filters and sort to work correctly per storefront (PRC-41)\nSFCC-19 Regional Storefronts — storefront configuration must be in place for Einstein to index per-region product and pricing data\nGlobal-e integration — international storefronts rely on Global-e pricing being available for display in autocomplete and search results\nSalesforce Einstein licence and SFCC environment provisioning — required before search development can begin\nUX/Design sign-off on two-panel autocomplete layout (SPR-38, SPR-39) — frontend build is design-dependent\nAssumptions & Constraints\nSalesforce Einstein fully replaces Searchspring/Athos Commerce across all 8 storefronts at go-live; no parallel search integration is in scope\nRules-based recommendation fallback will be in place at launch; Einstein AI recommendations activate as behavioural data accumulates post-launch\nAdd-to-bag toggle capability from recommendation carousels (SPR-62) is to be confirmed with the Zimmermann team\n\"Complete the Look\" cross-sell data (how looks are defined and associated) is a dependency on Zimmermann's product data setup\nSearch dictionary entries, Popular Search curation, and Einstein tuning are a Site Merchandiser responsibility post-launch\nAdditional recommendation surfaces beyond PDP and cart (e.g. PLP, Z.immerse, Find in Boutique) are TBC pending final designs (SPR-61)\nPriority:\n Medium\nTarget Release / Sprint:\n Sprint 3",
